<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Donnelly Mirrors expansion to create 190 Irish job.</title>
<headline>Donnelly Mirrors expansion to create 190 Irish job.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ireland's minister for enterprise and employment Richard Bruton on Monday announced that an expansion plan by Donnelly Mirrors Ltd will create up to 190 jobs over the next three years.</p>
<p>Bruton said in a statement that Donnelly Mirrors, a unit of Donnelly Corp, has agreed a new investment proposal with IDA Ireland, a state body set up to attract inward investment, which will result in 190 jobs being created at its Naas, Co Kildare plant.</p>
<p>Recruitment and training for some of the new positions has already begun, Bruton said.</p>
<p>-- Dublin newsroom + 353 1 676 9775</p>
